[38;5;231m[49m⏺[39m [1mSection 2 — UI behavior[0m

  [1mTheme.[0m The page has no CSS at all today, so this adds [38;5;153mstyles.css[39m: CSS custom properties for
  foreground/background/input colors on [38;5;153m:root[39m, overridden under [38;5;153m[data-theme="dark"][39m. Theme is applied by setting
  [38;5;153mdocument.documentElement.dataset.theme[39m. Nothing else in the page needs to know the theme exists.

  The load-order constraint from earlier drives the structure:

  - A [1msmall inline script in [38;5;153m<head>[0m reads the stored theme and sets [38;5;153mdata-theme[39m before the body renders. This is the one
    piece that cannot be deferred — if it moves to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m at the end of [38;5;153m<body>[39m, the page paints light and visibly flips.
    It's a few lines and duplicates a minimal read; that duplication is deliberate and gets a comment saying why.
  - [38;5;153mprefs.js[39m loads before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m via a normal [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag.
  - A [1mtoggle control[0m in the body — a checkbox labeled "Dark mode", wired in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m to [38;5;153mPrefs.set("theme", ...)[39m plus the
    [38;5;153mdataset.theme[39m update. Its checked state is initialized from [38;5;153mPrefs.get("theme")[39m on load, so it agrees with what the
    head script already did.

  [1mRemember username.[0m A checkbox next to the login form, "Remember my username", unchecked by default.

  - On successful [38;5;153mlogin()[39m, if the box is checked, store the username; if unchecked, clear it. Clearing on unchecked
    matters — otherwise unticking the box appears to do nothing until the next successful login.
  - On page load, if [38;5;153mrememberedUsername[39m is set, prefill [38;5;153m#username[39m and pre-check the box.
  - [1mThe password is never stored.[0m Worth stating explicitly in the spec because "remember me" is ambiguous in the wild
    and this is a login form.
  - Storing a username is mild PII on a shared device, which is why it is opt-in and why unticking clears immediately
    rather than lazily.

  [1mWhat this does not do:[0m no change to [38;5;153mlogin()[39m, [38;5;153mvalidateForm()[39m, or the submit flow beyond the one post-success hook.
  [38;5;153mlogin()[39m stays a stub. [38;5;153msrc/[39m is untouched.

  Does the UI behavior look right? Next section is tooling and testing, where I have a question for you.

